CHAPTER.VERS:
Woe to him that buildeth his house by 

          By bribes and extortion.
         unrighteousness, and his chambers by wrong; [that] useth his neighbour's service without wages, and giveth him not for his work;

[As] I live, saith the LORD, though 

          Who was called Jehoiachin or Jeconiah, whom he calls here Coniah in contempt who thought his kingdom could never depart from him, because he came of the stock of David, and therefore for the promise sake could not be taken from his house, but he abused God's promise and therefore was justly deprived of the kingdom.
         Coniah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah were the signet upon my right hand, yet would I pluck thee from there;
